//? Title: Prüfer codes: actual smallest leaves, decoding and exact enumeration
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Deleting the smallest available leaf and recording its neighbor gives one code
entry. The native encoder and decoder now retain their actual ordered leaf sets
at each removal. Complete tree validation prevents malformed graphs from
reaching an empty-set dereference. The original six-vertex tree and its code
3,3,3,4 remain, together with exact enumeration of all 16 four-vertex codes.
These discrete fixtures make every removal and the finite bijection check
inspectable.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

$$ \text{code length}=n-2,\qquad \#\text{labeled trees}=n^{n-2}\quad(n\ge2). $$

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/prufer_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    auto t = a::tree_to_prufer_trace(3, {{0, 1}, {1, 2}});
    const auto &s = t.steps[0];
    std::print("\n| actual leaves before | removed leaf | emitted neighbor | neighbor degree before | " "neighbor degree after | actual leaves after |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\n");
    std::print("| `{}` | {} | {} | {} | {} | `{}` |\n", s.leaves_before, s.leaf,
               s.neighbor, s.neighbor_degree_before, s.neighbor_degree_after,
               s.leaves_after);

    g::Diagram d;
    d.node("n0", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual smallest-leaf set\n{}", s.leaves_before));
    d.node("n1", {10, 0},
           std::format("Actual removal / emitted neighbor\n{} / {}", s.leaf,
                       s.neighbor));
    d.node("n2", {20, 0}, std::format("Actual next leaves\n{}", s.leaves_after));
    d.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    d.save_svg("build/prufer_tiny.svg");
}
```
