> API and interpretation

The ordinary encoder validates connectedness as well as n-1 edges and all
endpoints; a disconnected cycle or parallel-edge graph can no longer drive an
invalid leaf lookup. Ordered-set coding takes O(n log n) ordinary work, while
copied leaf-set histories may grow quadratically. Exhaustive enumeration is a
separate exponential exercise with checked integer powers and a sequence-count
cap; the mathematical Cayley count is labelled separately from the actually
decoded/distinct counts.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

> References

- H. Prüfer(1918), Neuer Beweis eines Satzes über Permutationen, Archiv der
  Mathematik und Physik, series3,27,142–144.

